diff -ruN a/SPARK-MACOS.md b/SPARK-MACOS.md
--- a/SPARK-MACOS.md
+++ b/SPARK-MACOS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# react-native-nitro-modules 1.0.0-alpha.nightly.100.g107f6fc66597, Legend Spark macOS port
+
+Moyo Learn for macOS runs on Legend Spark 0.0.2 (React Native macOS 0.83,
+CocoaPods). Spark ships Nitro 0.37.0 with its own patch; Moyo pins Nitro v1
+nightly.100 on every platform, so this is that nightly with the macOS parts of
+Spark's patch carried over, plus what v1 needs to build without SwiftPM.
+
+Upstream: `react-native-nitro-modules@1.0.0-alpha.nightly.100.g107f6fc66597`
+(npm integrity in `package.json` `spark.upstreamIntegrity`).
+
+## Changes
+
+1. **AppKit views** (from Spark's 0.37.0 patch). `apple/views/HybridView.swift`
+   declares `NitroPlatformView` as `UIView` or `NSView`, so `HybridView`
+   compiles on macOS.
+2. **Buildable podspec.** Upstream's podspec is metadata only. `NitroModules.podspec`
+   builds the sources Package.swift builds, for macOS 13+, through
+   `apple/cocoapods/nitro_cocoapods.rb`, which also gives nitrogen-generated
+   libraries their pod settings (`NitroCocoaPods.add_nitrogen_module`).
+   Spark's 0.37.0 patch moved the view template headers out of the public
+   headers; here every header is private and reaches Swift only through the
+   upstream module maps.
+3. **React Native 0.83 JSI.** `cpp/core/include/NitroModules/detail/JSICompat.hpp`
+   supplies `jsi::Array::push`, `jsi::Runtime::createError` and
+   `jsi::ArrayBuffer::tryGetMutableBuffer` (added after 0.83). Each helper
+   uses the JSI member when the headers have it, so the code is unchanged on 0.88.
+4. **simdutf-swift.** Upstream resolves margelo/simdutf-swift 1.0.1 through
+   SwiftPM. Here `NitroModules.podspec` depends on the `SimdUTF` pod from the
+   `simdutf-swift` package (Moyo's CocoaPods packaging of that tag, a peer
+   dependency of this port).
+5. **package.json.** `react-native` peer range widened to `>=0.83.0`, a peer
+   dependency on `simdutf-swift` 1.0.1, and the `spark` stamp Spark's
+   native-patch preflight reads.
+
+Not carried over from Spark's patch: the Windows adapter (`windows/`,
+`NITRO_WINDOWS_API` exports, react-native.config.js Windows entry). Moyo's
+desktop build is macOS only.
+
+The `.patch` file next to the tarball in the app is the diff of all of the
+above against upstream, except the `spark` stamp, which carries the patch's
+SHA-256 as `spark.patchHash`.
diff -ruN a/apple/cocoapods/nitro_cocoapods.rb b/apple/cocoapods/nitro_cocoapods.rb
--- a/apple/cocoapods/nitro_cocoapods.rb
+++ b/apple/cocoapods/nitro_cocoapods.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,224 @@
+# Legend Spark port of Nitro v1 (react-native-nitro-modules
+# 1.0.0-alpha.nightly.100.g107f6fc66597) for CocoaPods.
+#
+# Upstream v1 builds only through SwiftPM (Package.swift) and React Native
+# 0.88's `react-native spm`. Legend Spark 0.0.2 runs React Native macOS 0.83,
+# which installs native code with CocoaPods. This file turns the SwiftPM target
+# layout into pod settings, for NitroModules itself (`configure_nitro_modules`)
+# and for Nitro libraries generated by nitrogen (`add_nitrogen_module`), in
+# place of the `+autolinking.rb` file nitrogen 0.37 used to generate.
+#
+# SwiftPM keeps each Package.swift target as its own module. A pod is one Xcode
+# target with one Swift module, so the C++ targets become clang modules found
+# through module.modulemap files in header search directories: clang finds a
+# directory's module map while resolving its headers, and a module named M in
+# <dir>/M/module.modulemap when Swift imports M.
+#
+# Headers are therefore not pod source files. CocoaPods links every header in
+# source_files into Pods/Headers/{Public,Private}/<pod>, and those links come
+# first in the search paths. A header reached through a link is not the header
+# its module map names, so clang included it textually inside the module and
+# again through the module ("redefinition of 'BorrowingReference'" while
+# building NitroModulesAppleCxx). Headers ship through preserve_paths instead.
+#
+# One exception: NitroModulesAppleCxx.h is NitroModules' public header. Its
+# only content is includes of the two C++ modules, so the link is harmless,
+# and it puts their declarations into the CocoaPods umbrella of the NitroModules
+# clang module. That module also holds NitroModules-Swift.h (CocoaPods appends
+# it as NitroModules.Swift), whose C++ declarations name margelo::nitro types;
+# Swift does not include their headers, so without the umbrella every pod
+# importing NitroModules failed with "use of undeclared identifier 'margelo'".
+#
+# Paths into other packages are relative to ${PODS_ROOT}, so Podfile.lock
+# stays machine-independent.
+
+require "pathname"
+
+module NitroCocoaPods
+  PACKAGE_ROOT = File.expand_path("../..", __dir__)
+
+  # Each directory holds the module map of the clang module named beside it.
+  # Swift imports NitroModulesAppleCxx (which re-exports NitroModulesCxx). The
+  # swift-bridge and React Native directories have module maps too, but only
+  # C++ includes their headers, textually.
+  NITRO_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES = [
+    "cpp/core/include",              # NitroModulesCxx
+    "apple/core/include",            # NitroModulesAppleCxx
+    "apple/core/swift-bridge/include",
+    "include",
+  ].freeze
+
+  # SwiftPM's simdutf-swift dependency is the SimdUTF pod from the
+  # `simdutf-swift` package (a peer dependency of this port). Its Swift module
+  # imports the CSimdUTF clang module, so every pod that loads SimdUTF needs
+  # that package's cocoapods/ directory (CSimdUTF/module.modulemap) on its
+  # header search path.
+  SIMDUTF_PACKAGE = "simdutf-swift"
+
+  # Swift settings shared by NitroModules and generated libraries
+  # (Package.swift `NitroModules` target and nitrogen's `addNitrogenTargets`).
+  SWIFT_FLAGS = [
+    "-enable-upcoming-feature InternalImportsByDefault",
+    "-Xfrontend -clang-header-expose-decls=has-expose-attr-or-stdlib",
+  ].freeze
+
+  def self.quote(path)
+    "\"#{path}\""
+  end
+
+  # The Pods sandbox with symlinks resolved, without requiring it to exist.
+  # CocoaPods evaluates podspecs before it creates Pods/, so on a clean checkout
+  # Pathname#realpath on the sandbox raises ENOENT. Resolve the deepest ancestor
+  # that exists and append the missing components; once Pods/ exists the result
+  # equals Pathname#realpath. Nothing is written to disk.
+  def self.sandbox_realpath
+    path = Pathname.new(Pod::Config.instance.sandbox_root.to_s).expand_path
+    missing = []
+    until path.exist?
+      missing.unshift(path.basename)
+      path = path.dirname
+    end
+    missing.reduce(path.realpath) { |resolved, component| resolved + component }
+  end
+
+  # NitroModules' package root as seen from a dependent pod, e.g.
+  # ${PODS_ROOT}/../../node_modules/react-native-nitro-modules.
+  def self.package_root_from_pods
+    sandbox = sandbox_realpath
+    package = Pathname.new(PACKAGE_ROOT).realpath
+    "${PODS_ROOT}/#{package.relative_path_from(sandbox)}"
+  end
+
+  def self.simdutf_module_maps_from_pods
+    resolved = `node --print "require.resolve(process.argv[1] + '/package.json', { paths: [process.argv[2]] })" "#{SIMDUTF_PACKAGE}" "#{PACKAGE_ROOT}"`.strip
+    unless $?.success? && File.exist?(resolved)
+      raise "[NitroModules] #{SIMDUTF_PACKAGE} is not installed next to #{PACKAGE_ROOT}. It provides the SimdUTF pod Nitro v1 needs; add it to the app's dependencies."
+    end
+    sandbox = sandbox_realpath
+    "${PODS_ROOT}/#{Pathname.new(File.dirname(resolved)).realpath.relative_path_from(sandbox)}/cocoapods"
+  end
+
+  def self.merge_xcconfig(spec, settings)
+    current = spec.attributes_hash["pod_target_xcconfig"] || {}
+    merged = current.merge(settings) do |key, old, new|
+      key.start_with?("OTHER_") || key.end_with?("_PATHS") || key == "GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS" ? "#{old} #{new}" : new
+    end
+    spec.pod_target_xcconfig = merged
+  end
+
+  # Settings for NitroModules.podspec.
+  def self.configure_nitro_modules(spec)
+    root = "${PODS_TARGET_SRCROOT}"
+    spec.source_files = [
+      "apple/core/include/NitroModulesAppleCxx.h",
+      "cpp/core/src/**/*.cpp",
+      "apple/core/src/**/*.cpp",
+      "apple/core/core/**/*.swift",
+      "apple/core/utils/**/*.swift",
+      "apple/views/**/*.swift",
+      "apple/core/swift-bridge/src/**/*.cpp",
+      "cpp/src/**/*.cpp",
+      "apple/src/**/*.mm",
+    ]
+    spec.preserve_paths = [
+      "cpp/**/*.{h,hpp}",
+      "apple/**/*.{h,hpp}",
+      "include/**/*.{h,hpp}",
+      "**/module.modulemap",
+      "apple/cocoapods/**/*",
+    ]
+    spec.public_header_files = ["apple/core/include/NitroModulesAppleCxx.h"]
+    spec.dependency "SimdUTF"
+    # Package.swift: `.swiftLanguageMode(.v6)`. CocoaPods writes the pod's
+    # SWIFT_VERSION from swift_version, so it is set there as well as below.
+    spec.swift_version = "6.0"
+    merge_xcconfig(spec, {
+      "CLANG_CXX_LANGUAGE_STANDARD" => "c++20",
+      "SWIFT_VERSION" => "6.0",
+      # Swift C++ interoperability (Package.swift `.interoperabilityMode(.Cxx)`).
+      "SWIFT_OBJC_INTEROP_MODE" => "objcxx",
+      "SWIFT_APPROACHABLE_CONCURRENCY" => "YES",
+      "DEFINES_MODULE" => "YES",
+      # The Swift bridge includes NitroModules-Swift.h textually after the C++
+      # declarations it uses (Package.swift: `-fno-modules`). Swift itself
+      # still imports the clang modules through the module maps below.
+      "CLANG_ENABLE_MODULES" => "NO",
+      "HEADER_SEARCH_PATHS" => (NITRO_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES.map { |dir| "#{root}/#{dir}" } + [simdutf_module_maps_from_pods]).map { |dir| quote(dir) }.join(" "),
+      "GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS" => "NITRO_JSI_HAS_FAST_UTF16=0",
+      "OTHER_SWIFT_FLAGS" => (SWIFT_FLAGS + [
+        "-enable-upcoming-feature MemberImportVisibility",
+      ]).join(" "),
+    })
+  end
+
+  # Settings for a Nitro library generated by nitrogen v1, the CocoaPods
+  # counterpart of nitrogen's `addNitrogenTargets(to:)`.
+  #
+  # - module_name: nitro.json `apple.moduleName`; must equal the pod name.
+  # - module_maps_directory: a directory, relative to the podspec, holding
+  #   `<module_name>AppleCxx/module.modulemap`, which declares the clang module
+  #   over nitrogen/generated/apple/<module_name>AppleCxx/include. SwiftPM
+  #   derives that module from its target; CocoaPods needs it written down.
+  # - swift_sources / cxx_sources: as in addNitrogenTargets.
+  def self.add_nitrogen_module(spec, module_name:, module_maps_directory:, swift_sources: ["apple"], cxx_sources: ["cpp"])
+    unless spec.name == module_name
+      raise "[NitroModules] Pod #{spec.name} must be named after nitro.json apple.moduleName (#{module_name})."
+    end
+    # As in addNitrogenTargets, source directories that don't exist are skipped.
+    pod_root = File.dirname(spec.defined_in_file.to_s)
+    swift_sources = swift_sources.select { |dir| File.exist?(File.join(pod_root, dir)) }
+    apple_cxx_module_map = "#{module_maps_directory}/#{module_name}AppleCxx/module.modulemap"
+    unless File.exist?(File.join(pod_root, apple_cxx_module_map))
+      raise "[NitroModules] #{spec.name} needs #{apple_cxx_module_map} (see NitroCocoaPods.add_nitrogen_module)."
+    end
+    cxx_sources = cxx_sources.select { |dir| File.exist?(File.join(pod_root, dir)) }
+    nitro = package_root_from_pods
+    own = "${PODS_TARGET_SRCROOT}"
+    generated = "nitrogen/generated"
+    apple_cxx = "#{module_name}AppleCxx"
+
+    spec.dependency "NitroModules"
+    spec.source_files = Array(spec.attributes_hash["source_files"]) +
+      swift_sources.map { |dir| "#{dir}/**/*.swift" } +
+      cxx_sources.map { |dir| "#{dir}/**/*.{c,cpp,mm}" } + [
+        "#{generated}/shared/c++/**/*.cpp",
+        "#{generated}/apple/swift/**/*.swift",
+        "#{generated}/apple/c++/**/*.cpp",
+        "#{generated}/apple/#{apple_cxx}/**/*.cpp",
+        "#{generated}/apple/*.{cpp,mm}",
+      ]
+    # Headers reach the compiler through HEADER_SEARCH_PATHS only (see the top of this file).
+    spec.preserve_paths = Array(spec.attributes_hash["preserve_paths"]) + [
+      "#{generated}/**/*.{h,hpp}",
+      "#{generated}/**/module.modulemap",
+      "#{module_maps_directory}/**/*",
+      "nitro.json",
+    ] + cxx_sources.map { |dir| "#{dir}/**/*.{h,hpp}" }
+
+    spec.swift_version = "6.0"
+    merge_xcconfig(spec, {
+      "CLANG_CXX_LANGUAGE_STANDARD" => "c++20",
+      "SWIFT_VERSION" => "6.0",
+      "SWIFT_OBJC_INTEROP_MODE" => "objcxx",
+      "DEFINES_MODULE" => "YES",
+      # Same textual inclusion of <module>-Swift.h as NitroModules' bridge.
+      "CLANG_ENABLE_MODULES" => "NO",
+      "HEADER_SEARCH_PATHS" => ([
+        "#{own}/#{generated}/shared/c++/include",
+        "#{own}/#{generated}/apple/c++/include",
+        "#{own}/#{generated}/apple/#{apple_cxx}/include",
+        "#{own}/#{module_maps_directory}",
+      ] + cxx_sources.map { |dir| "#{own}/#{dir}" } +
+        NITRO_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES.map { |dir| "#{nitro}/#{dir}" } + [
+        simdutf_module_maps_from_pods,
+        # NitroModules-Swift.h, which NitroModules-Swift-Cxx-Umbrella.hpp includes.
+        "${PODS_CONFIGURATION_BUILD_DIR}/NitroModules/Swift Compatibility Header",
+      ]).map { |dir| quote(dir) }.join(" "),
+      "GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS" => "NITRO_JSI_HAS_FAST_UTF16=0",
+      "OTHER_SWIFT_FLAGS" => (SWIFT_FLAGS + [
+        # Keep declarations using NitroModules' Swift types in <module>-Swift.h.
+        "-Xfrontend -clang-header-expose-module -Xfrontend NitroModules=NitroModules-Swift.h",
+      ]).join(" "),
+    })
+  end
+end
